  "scope": "The literal480-slot original-row lambda machine reads its own selected original cost through the actual indexed rational reader, retains original dimension/exponent roots in a saved context, and feeds the literal returned cost record into the reviewed lambda core. The same physical run returns the exact original raw lambda fraction for a valid represented original index. All row fields, index/dimension/exponent words, source and heap prefix survive. The bound uses the original row bit sum, row length, index/dimension/exponent lengths and numerical exponent value; no binary-length-only exponent claim is made. No selected cost record or lambda intermediate is supplied. Initial representations, index validity, physical H/A and dense cursor remain explicit. Minimum selection, grid-derived exponent bounds and full guess/solver composition remain separate. Twelve physical cases independently specify exact raw outputs across first/later indices, duplicate rows, zero dimension and padded fields.",
  "pending": [
    "independent semantic review",
    "combined production integration and exact CI"
  ]
